WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.763
Operating local AI responsibly starts with intent.

00:00:02.763 --> 00:00:07.328
Define the workflow, choose an appropriate model, decide what data is allowed,

00:00:07.328 --> 00:00:09.230
and document the expected output.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.176
LM Studio can support local chat, model testing, and compatible local API workflows,

00:00:14.176 --> 00:00:17.980
but the surrounding process determines whether the result is dependable.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.165
Model choice should be based on task fit and hardware fit.

00:00:22.165 --> 00:00:25.209
Smaller models may be enough for routine assistance,

00:00:25.209 --> 00:00:28.252
while larger models may help when resources allow.

00:00:28.252 --> 00:00:29.774
Quantization, context length, speed,

00:00:29.774 --> 00:00:35.861
and quality should be evaluated with real prompts before the model is trusted for repeated use.

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:37.383
Data boundaries are central.

00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:41.567
Prompts, files, outputs, logs, exports, screenshots, and backups all need attention.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.752
Tool integrations and automation should start with low-risk tasks, narrow permissions,

00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:47.274
human review, and documentation.

00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:49.557
Finally, operate the workflow over time.

00:00:49.557 --> 00:00:53.361
Monitor performance, test updates, preserve important records, review model quality,

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:56.024
and retire integrations that no longer fit.

00:00:56.024 --> 00:00:59.828
Sovereign AI is not only about running a model locally.

00:00:59.828 --> 00:01:03.633
It is about control, accountability, evaluation, and repeatable operating habits.

00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:05.154
Start with small experiments,

00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:10.100
then add governance as the workflow becomes more valuable and more widely used.
